// @expect: true
// buzz declares pi in src/lib/math.buzz as the 14-digit literal 3.1415926535898,
// not the nearest double to pi. It is LESS precise than Go's math.Pi on purpose:
// pi is an observable constant, so deg/rad and everything built on them inherit
// its exact bits. With Go's value, math.deg(2.0) returned 114.59155902616465
// where buzz returns 114.59155902616439 - a silent difference for a program moved
// between the two (tests/behavior/math.buzz asserts the literal).
import "math";
final __r = math.deg(2.0) == 114.59155902616439 and math.rad(math.deg(2.0)) == 2;
